      "text": "To find the probability that both chosen members are girls, we can use combinations because the order in which the girls are chosen does not matter. The total number of ways to choose 2 members out of 10 is given by the combination formula \\( \\binom{n}{k} = \\frac{n!}{k!(n-k)!} \\).\n\nThe total number of ways to choose 2 members out of 10 is:\n\n\\[\n\\binom{10}{2} = \\frac{10!}{2!(10-2)!} = \\frac{10 \\times 9}{2 \\times 1} = 45\n\\]\n\nNow, the number of ways to choose 2 girls out of 5 is:\n\n\\[\n\\binom{5}{2} = \\frac{5!}{2!(5-2)!} = \\frac{5 \\times 4}{2 \\times 1} = 10\n\\]\n\nThe probability that both chosen members are girls is the ratio of the number of favorable outcomes to the total number of outcomes:\n\n\\[\nP(\\text{both girls}) = \\frac{\\binom{5}{2}}{\\binom{10}{2}} = \\frac{10}{45} = \\frac{2}{9}\n\\]\n\nLet's confirm this with Python code to ensure accuracy.\n```python\nimport math\r\n\r\n# Calculate the total number of ways to choose 2 members out of 10\r\ntotal_ways = math.comb(10, 2)\r\n\r\n# Calculate the number of ways to choose 2 girls out of 5\r\nways_to_choose_girls = math.comb(5, 2)\r\n\r\n# Calculate the probability that both chosen members are girls\r\nprobability = ways_to_choose_girls / total_ways\r\nprint(probability)\n```\n```output\n0.2222222222222222\n```\nThe probability that both chosen members are girls is \\(\\frac{2}{9}\\), which is approximately 0.2222. Therefore, the final answer is:\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{\\frac{2}{9}}\n\\]",
